    {
      "platform": "windows",
      "version": "1.6.6",
      "release_date": "2026-08-17",
      "release_notes": "What's Changed\n- Streamer Mode: fixed constantly re-enabling itself if OBS is open & fixed \"Automatically enable Streamer Mode\" toggle not showing in Discord appearance settings\n- Added a setting to work around Voice Chat not working when using VPNs like Tailscale\n- Fixed various issues related to screenshare with system audio on Linux\n- Upgraded to Electron43 which brings many fixes and improvements\n- Fixed an issue where the auto-start toggle would not accurately reflect its actual state on Windows\n- Added a --repair command line flag to quickly update Vencord to the latest version\nNotable Electron changes\n- On Linux, when using the custom Discord titlebar, Vesktop will now have rounded corners & shadow by default. You can disable this behaviour in Vesktop settings\n- On Linux, Vesktop will now show up as \"Vesktop\" instead of as \"Chromium\" in Audio mixers\nFor Linux users: It is now recommended to run Vesktop in native Wayland over legacy X11 for the best experience. You may run into graphical glitches when running on X11\nFull Changelog: v1.6.5...v1.6.6",
      "release_notes_url": "https://github.com/Vencord/Vesktop/releases/tag/v1.6.6",
